Source: ble.sh
Section: shells
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Dario Griffo <dariogriffo@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/akinomyoga/ble.sh
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: ble.sh
Architecture: all
Depends: procps, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: ble.sh-airline-themes
Description: Bash Line Editor -- a line editor written in pure Bash
 Bash Line Editor (ble.sh) is a command line editor written in pure Bash which
 replaces the default GNU Readline, enabling syntax highlighting, auto
 suggestions, vim modes, etc. in Bash interactive sessions.
 .
 This package ships the upstream nightly snapshot, which is already the
 generated install tree; at runtime it only needs ps (procps) beyond the
 essential packages.

Package: ble.sh-airline-themes
Architecture: all
Depends: ble.sh (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Airline themes for ble.sh
 Adopted from vim-airline's official theme collection and used by Bash Line
 Editor (ble.sh)'s imitation of the vim-airline status line.
